00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.540
POWER

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.540
SPEED

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.540
ENDURANCE

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.540
COST
PERFORMANCE

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.540
INTELLIGENCE

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.540
TECHNIQUE

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.040
<i>How'd I end up in this mess?</i>

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:07.220
Wolfie girl, your skin is so beautiful.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:08.810
I'm so jealous.

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:11.410
O-Oh, it's not that great...

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:13.670
Yours is much prettier, Lady Skylla.

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:16.680
Are you saying I'm beautiful?

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:18.060
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:21.840
Won't you leave yourself 
in my hands, Wolfie girl?

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:24.070
I'll be gentle with my washing.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:30.520
H-Hey! Th-That's a little too...

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:32.220
Stay still, now.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:34.150
Don't move.

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:36.370
R-Right!

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:39.710
How adorable you are, Wolfie girl!

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.500
I d-don't know about that...

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.090
Don't be afraid.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:46.290
You don't like this sort of thing?

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:49.780
I w-wouldn't say that, exactly...

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:53.640
You <i>like</i> it, then?

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:56.010
I w-wouldn't say that, either...

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:57.720
They're vulnerable!

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:58.590
Look out!

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.470
These don't look like your 
garden-variety peeping Toms.

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:06.290
We are heroes!

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:09.490
We strike down evil in the name of justice!

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.870
What the hell kind of heroes 
bust into the girls' bath

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:14.860
and start swingin' blades without 
even introducin' themselves?!

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:17.470
Well, if we declared ourselves 
the Assassin Rangers first,

00:14:17.470 --> 00:14:19.080
we wouldn't be very good assassins.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.490
What he said!

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:21.490
Not my problem!

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:25.070
Now, sit back and be assassinated!

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:31.120
You've ruined my time with 
my precious Wolfie girl...

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.260
And now you shall pay!

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:36.650
I'll tear you to shreds!

00:14:39.380 --> 00:14:41.230
Th-The beasts!

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:43.030
What is this monster?!

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:45.290
Bete Claw!

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.890
Guess I'd better call the others.

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.250
Come now, Wolfie girl.

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:59.090
I'll get you nice and clean again.

00:14:59.090 --> 00:15:02.350
<i>I guess the danger's not 
over for me, though!</i>

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:06.670
Boy, this is nice.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:16.810
<b>Foot Bath
Adult 100  Child 50</b>

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:16.810
<b>Day
Trip
Foot
 Bath</b>

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:09.160
True bliss.

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:14.450
Should our freezing combat executive 
be warming up in a foot bath?

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:16.810
Maybe I'll join you.

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:21.700
This is a foot bath. What do
 you think you're doing?

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:25.410
This is the only way I can get my feet in.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:28.090
Could stand to be hotter, though.

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:30.060
Maybe I'll heat it up a bit...

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.030
They fell for it!

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:39.290
Assassin Ninja Technique, Inferno Escape!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:41.440
I said it could stand to be hotter...

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.090
But that's a little extreme, don't you think?

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:46.420
What?!

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:50.160
I'm designed to deal with 
extreme temperatures.

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:52.960
Your fire can't do squat against me.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:57.880
What?! I can't move!

00:15:57.880 --> 00:15:58.970
They tricked us!

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:00.340
Damn it!

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:02.990
What's with the wannabe ninjas?

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:05.370
Is this supposed to be some 
kind of entertainment?

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:07.820
I've received a report from Uncle.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:10.300
They appear to be a minor hero gang.

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:14.500
You call yourselves the Assassin Rangers, 
but your work is terribly sloppy!

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:19.380
Only a hack would show up to boast 
seconds after springing a trap!

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:23.080
And you completely failed 
to mask your presences!

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:26.870
I knew you were there from the start!

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:32.070
You knew, but you still let 
me trigger their trap?

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:34.800
Better than an innocent civilian doing it!

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:38.060
Now, line up!

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.570
I'll teach you the 
fundamentals of espionage!

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:43.260
You'll want to take notes, too!

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:45.310
Uh, we don't have notepads...

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:48.540
Then go buy some at that souvenir shop!

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:50.640
Dash!

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:51.460
I ended up with a real pain in the rear.

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:52.330
D-Dash?! R-Right!

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:00.460
Not bad at all, Jaguar!

00:17:01.090 --> 00:17:03.870
When I fight, I never lose!

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:05.430
Your resolve is impressive.

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:08.330
Then let's kick it up a notch!

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:09.830
Sounds good to me!

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:24.380
Look at you, keeping up with me!

00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:27.920
I'm not the Jaguar I once was!

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:32.070
You guys are awfully fired up over 
a little game of ping-pong.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:36.270
Who are these people?

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:40.460
Uncle's investigation revealed them 
to be a group of lesser heroes

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:42.290
with a headquarters nearby.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:45.020
"Assassin Rangers Jyuyushi."

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:48.230
It looks like they're up to 
some pretty radical things.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:52.300
I doubt the world would get behind 
an assassination-based hero team.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:55.680
The only true justice is the dispatch of evil!

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:58.150
The methods don't matter!

00:17:58.150 --> 00:17:59.680
Actually, methods are very important.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:02.900
Running an operation like that costs money.

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:06.440
You can't run an organization 
without everyone's cooperation.

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:10.330
Evil is unworthy of speaking such just words!

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.060
Prepare to die!

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:22.520
I guess the Philadelphia Plan
 is running smoothly.

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:24.090
Are you all right?

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:27.340
You're so awesome, Lord Eldridge!

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:30.180
I suppose I am!

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:35.010
By the way, I think a flaw in the system 
is giving me selective amnesia.

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:37.090
Who exactly are you?

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:43.660
The Plan's still got some 
bugs to work out, huh?

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:45.760
Curse you!

00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:47.460
But this isn't over!

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:49.900
We still have an ace up our sleeve!

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:06.330
Hey, look! They sent out a robot!

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:09.700
Yeah, they definitely got 
that one second-hand.

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:13.870
Some other hero team must've had it before.

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:15.260
What do we do?

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:19.810
You'd probably only need three of us 
together to take out a second-hand robot.

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:22.660
No, wait.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.020
I hear something.

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:28.020
You're all finished!

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:32.470
It's a cornerstone of justice, 
even if it means hurting civilians!

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:35.450
This isn't good.

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:37.870
We've got to get the civilians to safety!

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:39.980
No, we'll be fine.

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:42.330
It seems he came along, as well.

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:49.870
<b>Curse Dragon Executive
Fáfnir</b>

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:06.890
Fáfnir...

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:09.260
I didn't know he was coming today!

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:12.100
He wants to come every time,

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:14.910
but there are operational costs 
that come up when he moves around.

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:16.640
Hey, we did it!

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:20.830
Actually, who's that big guy?

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:24.800
The Philadelphia Plan really is dicey.

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:28.720
What a dodgy bunch of heroes.

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:31.910
But the people seem to think it was a show,

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:33.540
so I guess it's okay.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:36.530
Hey! Wave to the people, Fáfnir!

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:47.520
<i>And so, despite a few minor bumps in the road,
 the employee retreat was a success.</i>

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.400
<i>Or so they believed...</i>

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:52.470
Miss Kuroitsu...

00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:55.600
I never wanna go to one of those again!

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:59.980
Maybe next time we'll go 
somewhere, just you and me.

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:02.840
Just you and me?!

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:12.330
Take that! And that, and that!

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.620
You jerk! You big loser!

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:18.630
<b>Secret Society: Agastia Great Leader
Akashic</b>

00:21:14.630 --> 00:21:15.890
You traitor!

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:17.720
Leaving me off on my own like that...

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:20.120
You're really gonna pay!

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.270
What's up?

00:21:26.560 --> 00:21:27.830
Who're you?

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:32.410
Well, actually... I play that game, too.

00:21:35.990 --> 00:21:37.270
You got left behind?

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:39.230
Yeah, I'm all alone.

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:41.390
The others are off on a really fun trip.

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:43.960
That sounds pretty lonely.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:45.790
Well, I'm not lonely at all!

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:47.020
I'm fine.

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:49.880
I just hate being left behind.

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:51.850
You're a strong person.

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:53.270
Of course I am!

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:54.760
I'm the strongest there is.

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:56.420
I'm jealous.

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:57.670
How come?

00:21:57.670 --> 00:22:01.660
I'm not strong at all. 
I'm always lonely, too.

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:03.360
You don't have any friends?

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:06.620
Oh, here it comes! Hurry!

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:07.930
Uh-oh!

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:12.930
I guess my senpai at work 
is kind of like a friend.

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:14.720
Is she nice?

00:22:14.720 --> 00:22:16.240
I think so...

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:22.310
Yes! We won! I've never gotten 
past this part before!

00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:24.180
You're really good at this!

00:22:25.300 --> 00:22:26.270
Oh, hey...

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:29.450
<b>Cream Roll
50% price as marked</b>

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:29.460
Wanna split it?

00:22:31.350 --> 00:22:32.460
Sure!

00:22:38.130 --> 00:22:39.880
Yes? Mizuki here.

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:42.000
<i>You're free, right, Mizuki?</i>

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:45.000
<i>I got a call from a new employer.</i>

00:22:57.630 --> 00:22:58.820
Attention, all!

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:00.150
Allow me to introduce...

00:23:01.370 --> 00:23:04.840
Agastia's newest executives,

00:23:04.840 --> 00:23:07.730
Karen Mizuki and Heiki Matsuyama!

00:23:08.340 --> 00:23:10.730
All glory to Agastia!

00:23:10.980 --> 00:23:13.240
All glory to Agastia!

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:15.120
All glory to Agastia!

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:16.650
Glory!

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:18.510
Glory!

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:20.600
Glory!

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:20.600
I'm counting on you two!

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:28.260
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:31.800
Join us next time for the final episode of <i>Miss 
Kuroitsu of the Monster Development Department</i>!

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:32.000
<b>Those Sacrifices Saved from Hell by
a Black-Winged Devil That Devours Other
 Devils Will Revere It as God Regardless
 of Whether Its Act Makes It a Servant
 of Heaven or Merely a Savage Cannibal</b>
